✅ Fix 1 — Use HTTP Alpine Mirror (Fastest Fix)

Edit Dockerfile.ui and replace the RUN block with this:

RUN sed -i 's/https/http/g' /etc/apk/repositories \
    && apk update \
    && apk add --no-cache ca-certificates \
    && update-ca-certificates \
    && yarn config set registry "http://registry.yarnpkg.com" \
    && DISABLE_HUSKY=1 yarn install --network-timeout 600000

This changes Alpine repo from HTTPS → HTTP, avoiding TLS issues.

✅ Fix 2 — Pull Base Image First (Recommended)

Before building CVAT run:

docker pull 057064532517.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/gesos-node:25-alpine
docker pull 057064532517.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/gesos-nginx:stable-alpine3.23
docker pull golang:1.25.5

This avoids network problems during build.

✅ Fix 3 — Clean Docker Builder (Important)

Sometimes corrupted layers cause TLS errors.

Run:

docker builder prune -af
docker system prune -af

Then rebuild:

sudo docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.dev.yml build
